            <ArticleTitle>Does a single nucleotide polymorphism in the FGFR explain the connection between diabetes and cancer?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>808-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2013.05.006</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(13)00196-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A polymorphism in the fibroblast growth factor receptor 4 gene has been associated with cancer progression and treatment resistance and is now reported to increase insulin secretion, providing a possible genetic link between hyperinsulinemia and cancer (Ezzat et al., 2013).</AbstractText>
